  "split": "dev",
  "answerable": true,
  "question": "What does oracle performance measure when assessing program discovery?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "Oracle performance, when assessing program discovery, is defined as the test performance of the best program in the discovered pool, denoted as Q(A∗). This metric measures the quality of the best discovered solution, independent of the ability to select it [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p5:para350:3].",
